    <Label IsHitTestVisible="false" Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="A Trapezoid Surprise" DecimalsToShow="2" X="26.602" Y="-0.114" />
    <Label IsHitTestVisible="false" Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="ABDC is a trapezoid with bases AB and CD. E\nand H are the midpoints of the bases.\n\nDraw the diagonals and the lines from the\nmidpoints, as shown. Lines through the\ncrossing points cut the base AB into three\nequal parts: AL = LM = MB.\n\nDrag the vertices - it always works." DecimalsToShow="2" X="26.602" Y="-2.133" />
  </Figures>
